# Lima 3.10 backport - defconfig delta, verified against gtel3g_defconfig
# (gtel3g/kernel_samsung_gtel3g, branch lineage-16.0 = Linux 3.10.103)
#
# 1. Vendor driver OFF (built-in in the stock defconfig; unsetting MALI400
#    drops the whole mali400 option block):
# CONFIG_MALI400 is not set
#
# 2. lima + DRM core ON (stock defconfig has "# CONFIG_DRM is not set"):
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_LIMA=m
#
# 3. Keep the rest of the stock graphics config unchanged:
#    CONFIG_ION=y / CONFIG_ION_SPRD=y   (Android still uses ION for gralloc;
#                                      lima PRIME works next to it)
#    CONFIG_SPRD_IOMMU=y               (used by camera/video blocks; the
#                                      vendor mali driver does NOT use it
#                                      for the GPU - verified - and lima
#                                      drives the Mali's internal MMU)
#    # CONFIG_CMA is not set           (fine; lima does not need CMA)
#    # CONFIG_MODVERSIONS is not set   (recommended while iterating: avoids
#                                      the genksyms host-tool dependency)
